tion out of seeing  billionaire investor and prominent  Democratic support urge or cirrhosis  quote dead bloated corpse being dragged  through the streets etc etc and  ultimately CNN put out an article  explaining that they actually tracked  down who this person was in real life  and they put out a statement about their  decision not to release the person's  identity and we're going to get to that  in a second so so far I wasn't offended  by this by this video I didn't find  anything particularly remarkable it's  kind of funny but it really did not seem  like a huge deal I mean yes the  president is retweeting something so  stupid but this is what he does Trump  tweets about stuff that's meaningless  while but you know while pulling out of  the Paris climate Accord that's not new  yeah I mean some may call it an attack  on the media but I think that's kind of  a flaccid critique because pretty much  everyone knows that wrestling is fake  and this is all just in good fun  but this is not the first time that  Donald Trump has retweeted content from  someone who regularly puts up  anti-semitic and racist material your  the black on black versus white on white  crime statistics your Hillary Clinton  with a that star of david' that said  most corrupt politician ever tour so it  long and short of it is yes this is sort  of weird behavior for a 71 year old man  or 70 year old man however old he is at  this point but it is consistent with his  past behavior so CNN tracks down who  this person that made the video is in  real life and they put out an article  saying quote CNN is not publishing on a  whole so loes name that's the reddit  username because he is a private citizen  who has issued an extensive statement of  apology showed his remorse by saying he  has taken down all his offending posts  and because he said he is not going to  repeat this ugly behavior on social  media again in addition he said his  statement could serve as an example to  others not to do the same 